 11.\n$x=3$: $3^2=9$, $3^4=81\\equiv 81-7\\times11=81-77=4$, $3^5=4\\times3=12\\equiv 1$. $5x^2=5\\times9=45\\equiv 1$. $x+1=4$. Total: $1+1+4=6$. No. ✓ (matches my earlier 6)\n\n$x=4$: $4^2=16\\equiv 5$, $4^4\\equiv 25\\equiv 3$, $4^5\\equiv 3\\times4=12\\equiv 1$. $5\\times5=25\\equiv 3$. $x+1=5$. Total: $1+3+5=9$. No. ✓\n\n$x=5$: $5^2=25\\equiv 3$, $5^4\\equiv 9$, $5^5\\equiv 9\\times5=45\\equiv 1$. $5\\times3=15\\equiv 4$. $x+1=6$. Total: $1+4+6=11\\equiv 0$. Yes. ✓\n\n$x=6\\equiv -5$: $f(-5)=(-5)^5+5(25)+(-5)+1=-3125+125-5+1=-3004$. $-3004 \\mod 11$: $3004/11=273.09$, $11\\times273=3003$, $-3004\\equiv -(3004)\\equiv -(3003+1)\\equiv -1\\equiv 10$. No. ✓\n\n$x=7\\equiv -4$: $f(-4)=-1024+80-4+1=-947$. $947/11=86.09$, $11\\times86=946$, $-947\\equiv -1\\equiv 10$. No. ✓\n\n$x=8\\equiv -3$: $f(-3)=-243+45-3+1=-200$. $200/11=18.18$, $11\\times18=198$, $-200\\equiv -2\\equiv 9$. No. ✓\n\n$x=9\\equiv -2$: $f(-2)=-32+20-2+1=-13\\equiv -2\\equiv 9$. No. ✓\n\n$x=10\\equiv -1$: $f(-1)=-1+5-1+1=4$. No. ✓\n\nGreat, so exactly 2 roots mod 11: $x\\equiv 2$ and $x\\equiv 5$, both with $f'$ nonzero mod 11, so each lifts uniquely to one root mod 121.\n\nTotal: 2 solutions.\n\nLet me also double check the derivative values mod 11 to make sure they're nonzero:\n$f'(2) = 5(16)+10(2)+1 = 101 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11}$. Nonzero. ✓\n$f'(5) = 5(625)+50+1 = 3176 \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}$. Nonzero. ✓\n\nBoth lift uniquely. Answer is 2.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786670885}
